 ## Overview
-This method defines a composite objective function for the joint optimization of a Template-Free NeRF (TFS-NeRF), an Implicit Neural Network (INN) for spatial transformation, and a skinning weight prediction network. It solves the ambiguity in dynamic scene reconstruction where incorrect combinations of canonical points and skinning weights can satisfy forward Linear Blend Skinning (LBS) equations [S1]. It distinguishes itself by explicitly constraining the INN and skinning networks through pose, cycle consistency, and skinning weight losses, rather than relying solely on photometric reconstruction [S1].
+This method defines a composite objective function for the joint optimization of a Template-Free NeRF (TFS-NeRF), an Implicit Neural Network (INN) for spatial transformation, and a skinning weight prediction network [S1]. It solves the ambiguity in dynamic scene reconstruction where incorrect combinations of canonical points and skinning weights can satisfy forward Linear Blend Skinning (LBS) equations [S1]. It distinguishes itself by explicitly constraining the INN and skinning networks through pose, cycle consistency, and skinning weight losses, rather than relying solely on photometric reconstruction [S1].
 
 ## How it works
-The method optimizes three coupled components simultaneously: the NeRF for appearance, the INN for mapping between view and canonical spaces, and a skinning weight network for deformation [S1].
+**Inputs:** Input video frames with known camera poses, canonical skeleton joints $J_{p0}$, deformed skeleton joints $J_p$, and point clouds initialized around the canonical skeleton of individual entities [S1].
 
-**Inputs:**
